WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
A clinical trial found daily fiber eased knee-ostiarthritis pain and improved strength. This is Longevity Weekly, episode 6, the science of aging, read carefully, never medical advice. After that trial, a bone density paper on statins, then a first human reprogramming read out, then what an aging biomarker has to prove. Science Daily's clinical trial is the fiber finding, and it sits in people, not in mice. A daily fiber supplement also made the body less sensitive to pain. Researchers said

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:33.780
gut bacteria and the hormone GLP1 may sit behind those changes.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:39.680
That hormone link is a proposed path, not a demonstration that GLP1 caused the relief.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:44.720
Nothing in these sources shows a regulator has approved fiber for an aging-related use.

00:00:45.803 --> 00:00:50.043
Yang and colleagues, writing in nature aging, found statin use lined up with a slower

00:00:50.043 --> 00:00:53.003
yearly drop in bone mineral density after menopause.

00:00:53.443 --> 00:00:58.303
That piece is an observational association, not a randomized test of bone outcomes.

00:00:58.303 --> 00:01:04.003
In the same paper, a torvostatin pushed bone building only when estrogen was low, by

00:01:04.003 --> 00:01:07.663
steering leptin receptor-positive marrow stromal cells toward bone.

00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:11.243
Those cells include skeletal stem and progenitor cells.

00:01:11.823 --> 00:01:17.903
The experimental root was less rack-1 prenalation, then nuclear factor capa B turning on own,

00:01:18.503 --> 00:01:20.103
and more osteoblasts.

00:01:20.483 --> 00:01:25.583
Estrogen hits the same cells through estradiol and estrogen receptor alpha, also turning

00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:30.903
on own, so the statin path is described as a stand-in for a signal menopause weakens.

00:01:31.383 --> 00:01:35.843
The authors placed this beside cholesterol management, and this paper does not establish

00:01:35.843 --> 00:01:37.563
an aging-related bone approval.

00:01:38.083 --> 00:01:44.363
They also note that older observational statin-and-bone studies have disagreed by cohort, endpoint, and design.

00:01:45.446 --> 00:01:52.866
Life biosciences told LifeSpan.io it has interim data from a Phase 1 trial of ER-100 in 3 participants.

00:01:52.866 --> 00:01:58.206
Since October 14, that is the first human step this show had been waiting on for partial

00:01:58.206 --> 00:01:59.086
reprogramming.

00:01:59.466 --> 00:02:03.886
The company is described there as working on cellular rejuvenation medicines for diseases

00:02:03.886 --> 00:02:04.526
of aging.

00:02:05.006 --> 00:02:09.886
A fight-aging newsletter called the same announcement initial results from the first reprogramming

00:02:09.886 --> 00:02:10.226
trial.

00:02:10.886 --> 00:02:16.046
Interim data in three people is an early human trial note, not a published efficacy result,

00:02:16.286 --> 00:02:20.146
an approval of ER-100 for an aging use is not established here.

00:02:20.146 --> 00:02:25.268
Professor Walter Longo, head of the Longevity Institute at the University of Southern

00:02:25.268 --> 00:02:29.148
California, told the independent which low-cost habits he favors.

00:02:29.688 --> 00:02:34.648
He named a mostly plant-based pattern with some fish and little meat, meals inside a daily

00:02:34.648 --> 00:02:37.268
window, regular exercise, and better sleep.

00:02:37.788 --> 00:02:43.308
That is an expert interview, not a new randomized trial, and no longevity diet is shown here

00:02:43.308 --> 00:02:44.488
as regulator approved.

00:02:45.008 --> 00:02:50.488
He said a 12-hour window curbs excess eating and side steps fast of 16 hours or longer

00:02:50.488 --> 00:02:54.128
sensor, which he said some research ties to higher heart disease risk.

00:02:54.548 --> 00:02:59.328
His longevity diet, the interview notes, inspired Michael Mosley's 5-2 diet.

00:03:00.318 --> 00:03:05.378
A fight aging review of the aging gut says thousands of microbial species shift with age.

00:03:05.938 --> 00:03:10.898
Microbes that stir chronic inflammation gain ground on microbes that make useful metabolites.

00:03:11.438 --> 00:03:16.958
Human population maps, the piece says, have correlated microbiome features and metabolites

00:03:16.958 --> 00:03:21.818
with age-related diseases, and osteoporosis is expected to have many such links.

00:03:22.378 --> 00:03:27.438
Those are correlations in a review, not a trial that changing gut microbes prevents fractures.

00:03:28.314 --> 00:03:35.894
Fight aging also reports a xenomorphic microRNA, MIR-3155B, found while researchers tried to

00:03:35.894 --> 00:03:38.694
lighten the senescent cell load left by cancer therapy.

00:03:39.474 --> 00:03:44.774
Senomorphic in that account means damping inflammatory signals from senescent cells rather than

00:03:44.774 --> 00:03:46.394
killing them or slowing their birth.

00:03:46.394 --> 00:03:52.834
Earth. This is a pre-clinical discovery report, and regulatory approval of MIR-3155B is

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:58.377
not established. AOL reported that fish oil supplements failed a major test for memory

00:03:58.377 --> 00:04:04.177
and brain aging. Fight aging writes that aging microglia turned more inflammatory, feeding

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:08.717
chronic brain inflammation that can disrupt function and feed neurodegenerative disease,

00:04:09.177 --> 00:04:11.777
and that senescence explains only part of the shift.

00:04:11.777 --> 00:04:18.037
LifeSpan.io says repair therapies built to hit several age-related diseases at once are

00:04:18.037 --> 00:04:20.557
still forced down existing regulatory pathways.

00:04:21.017 --> 00:04:25.877
This week's mechanism is biomarkers of aging, and the sharpest new measurement is a blood

00:04:25.877 --> 00:04:27.577
study, not a clock product.

00:04:28.297 --> 00:04:33.017
Incognitively unimpaired adults, neurobiology of aging modeled how inflammation markers

00:04:33.017 --> 00:04:34.497
in blood relate to each other.

00:04:35.077 --> 00:04:41.757
A network centered on CXCl5 tracked age, sex, and the cerebrospinal fluid ratio of amyloid

00:04:41.757 --> 00:04:44.237
Beta 42 to Amaloid Beta 40.

00:04:44.657 --> 00:04:47.977
That is observational network analysis, not a treatment trial.

00:04:48.477 --> 00:04:53.897
The authors broke networks into eigenvectors with hub proteins, then tested those eigenproteins

00:04:53.897 --> 00:04:59.157
against demographics, Alzheimer's markers in spinal fluid and blood, and immune history.

00:04:59.737 --> 00:05:04.757
A science-china life sciences review defines an aging biomarker as parameters that gauge

00:05:04.757 --> 00:05:09.697
age-related change, follow physiological aging, and flag a turn toward disease.

00:05:09.697 --> 00:05:15.537
The same review says the practical questions are how old the body is, why it ages, and how

00:05:15.537 --> 00:05:16.617
that pace might slow.

00:05:17.177 --> 00:05:23.517
It sorts markers into physiology, medical imaging, histology, cellular change, molecular change,

00:05:23.717 --> 00:05:24.937
and secreted factors.

00:05:25.457 --> 00:05:29.677
A useful one it argues is specific, systemic, and clinically relevant.

00:05:30.097 --> 00:05:33.637
And it says uses and limits of today's set are still poorly mapped.

00:05:34.277 --> 00:05:37.477
That paper is a review framework, not a validation experiment.

00:05:37.477 --> 00:05:42.637
A cell paper says these markers are how the field hopes to judge longevity interventions

00:05:42.637 --> 00:05:46.977
in people on a human time scale, including as possible surrogate endpoints.

00:05:47.257 --> 00:05:52.557
It also says there is no agreed list of what makes an aging biomarker reliable, and that

00:05:52.557 --> 00:05:54.257
gap blocks clinical validation.

00:05:54.897 --> 00:06:00.357
The authors offer language, classes, and possible clinic uses, plus validation steps and

00:06:00.357 --> 00:06:01.317
unsolved problems.

00:06:01.857 --> 00:06:06.397
A Nature Medicine review of Omic markers says the field still lacks a shared rule for

00:06:06.397 --> 00:06:11.817
validation before the clinic. It looks at predictive checks in population studies, warns

00:06:11.817 --> 00:06:16.537
that studies are hard to compare and hard to generalize, and says orderly validation could

00:06:16.537 --> 00:06:21.997
speed gerotherapeutic trials. None of those reviews is a trial, and none says a regulator

00:06:21.997 --> 00:06:27.197
has accepted a clock or a blood network as an approval endpoint for aging. The inflammation

00:06:27.197 --> 00:06:33.297
paper is a warning against one blood number as biological age. An interleukin-6 and FGF-21

00:06:33.297 --> 00:06:39.537
network tracked sex, the spinal fluid amyloid ratio, and q-alb, the spinal fluid to serum

00:06:39.537 --> 00:06:46.357
albumin ratio, and interferon gamma and CxCl9 network tracked both age and that spinal fluid

00:06:46.357 --> 00:06:47.317
amyloid ratio.

00:06:47.977 --> 00:06:56.737
Networks built on CxCl11 with CxCl9, and on CxCl19 with CxCl4, tracked sex alone, a network

00:06:56.737 --> 00:07:02.777
of MCP3, MCP4, and CXCL6 tracked how many surgeries a person had accumulated.

00:07:03.477 --> 00:07:09.577
Plasma Amaloid Beta 42 over 40 did not significantly track any of those blood inflammation networks,

00:07:10.137 --> 00:07:11.637
even where spinal fluid did.

00:07:12.277 --> 00:07:16.877
The authors say reading immune biology from blood is important and hard, because these

00:07:16.877 --> 00:07:21.217
markers do many jobs and stick to several demographic and health facts at once.

00:07:21.217 --> 00:07:27.757
A review in Ravista de Investigación Clinica starts from a plane fact, people born the

00:07:27.757 --> 00:07:29.797
same year do not age on one path.

00:07:30.377 --> 00:07:36.557
Neuronal markers, scans, blood tests, and vessel measures are described as capturing neurodegeneration,

00:07:37.257 --> 00:07:40.197
neuroinflammation, vessel failure, and weak resilience.

00:07:40.837 --> 00:07:50.177
Behavioral markers, gate, mobility, dual task performance, balance, activity, sleep, and

00:07:50.177 --> 00:07:52.997
biological changes showing up and what a person can do.

00:07:53.617 --> 00:07:56.177
The review says shifts in these markers may come years

00:07:56.177 --> 00:07:59.317
before cognitive decline, frailty, disability,

00:07:59.717 --> 00:08:00.737
and lost independence.

00:08:01.297 --> 00:08:04.137
That may is a review summary, not a new count

00:08:04.137 --> 00:08:05.197
from a named cohort.

00:08:06.017 --> 00:08:07.717
Putting neuronal markers, behavior,

00:08:07.997 --> 00:08:09.437
and physical performance together,

00:08:09.897 --> 00:08:11.577
might flag riskier trajectories

00:08:11.577 --> 00:08:13.877
and serve precision neuroscience aimed

00:08:13.877 --> 00:08:15.077
at intrinsic capacity.

00:08:15.737 --> 00:08:17.637
The authors say those combined models

00:08:17.637 --> 00:08:20.097
still need testing in clinics and in populations.

00:08:20.877 --> 00:08:26.637
The oldest paper here is a 1999 account of the biomarkers of aging program at the National

00:08:26.637 --> 00:08:30.917
Center for Toxicological Research and the National Institute on Aging.

00:08:31.457 --> 00:08:36.377
The goal was a rodent panel for asking whether an intervention slows aging, on a bet that

00:08:36.377 --> 00:08:40.037
a marker working across genotypes and species might matter in people.

00:08:40.777 --> 00:08:42.917
Chaloric restriction was the lifespan model.

00:08:42.917 --> 00:08:49.817
The program logged more than 60,000 individually housed animals, 7 mouse and rat genotypes, both

00:08:49.817 --> 00:08:53.577
sexes, about half eating freely and half calorie restricted.

00:08:54.197 --> 00:08:58.497
That is animal infrastructure, not proof a rodent marker predicts a human outcome.

00:08:59.257 --> 00:09:02.717
What these papers do not establish is a shared pass-fail test.

00:09:03.137 --> 00:09:09.077
Arregulators yes to any omit clock or inflammation network as a stand-in for health span or lifespan.

00:09:09.077 --> 00:09:13.777
or proof that changing in network changes dementia, frailty, or survival.

00:09:14.317 --> 00:09:16.577
The tightest limit is the blood study itself.

00:09:17.117 --> 00:09:22.177
Networks followed a spinal fluid amyloid ratio and did not follow the same ratio in plasma,

00:09:22.837 --> 00:09:24.837
in adults who were still cognitively well.

00:09:25.773 --> 00:09:29.773
One thing worth knowing is that a human trial tied a daily fiber supplement

00:09:29.773 --> 00:09:33.053
to less knee osteoarthritis pain and more strength.

00:09:33.473 --> 00:09:37.593
So later life joint symptoms are being studied as something gut signals may track.

00:09:37.593 --> 00:09:42.793
Staten use in postmenopausal women lined up with slower yearly bone density loss,

00:09:43.173 --> 00:09:46.893
and that remains an association sitting next to experimental cell work,

00:09:47.213 --> 00:09:49.493
not proof a cholesterol drug saves bone.

00:09:50.173 --> 00:09:53.013
Blood inflammation networks in cognitively well-adults

00:09:53.013 --> 00:09:55.273
followed a spinal fluid amyloid ratio.

00:09:55.853 --> 00:09:57.733
The same study did not see in plasma,

00:09:58.213 --> 00:10:01.593
so a blood marker is not automatically the spinal fluid measurement.

00:10:02.193 --> 00:10:03.473
A clinical review says,

00:10:03.473 --> 00:10:08.633
neuronal and behavioral marker changes may arrive years before frailty or lost independence.

00:10:09.193 --> 00:10:13.133
And it also says the combined models are not validated for clinic use yet.

00:10:13.673 --> 00:10:14.913
That's longevity weekly.

00:10:15.513 --> 00:10:17.733
This show is education, not medical advice.

00:10:18.313 --> 00:10:21.093
Talk to your own clinician before acting on anything you heard.

